    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14048" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĭōbŏlāris</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		vox hibr., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διώβολον</span>, with ending
			-aris, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that costs</i> or <i>is worth two</i> oboli: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scorta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Poen. 1, 2, 58</span></i>
			; cf. id. Fragm. ap. <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 64</span></i>; Paul. ex
				<i><span class="en">Fest. p. 74, 6</span></i> Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 2, 2, 64</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĭōbŏlārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>the title of a
				comedy</i> otherwise unknown, <i><span class="en">Fulg. 566,
				7</span></i>.</div>
